        "explanation": "<p><i>Dry rot</i> is a biological defect caused by fungi that thrive in damp, poorly ventilated conditions. It breaks down the cellulose in timber, leading to structural weakness and decay. Other biological defects include wet rot and insect attacks (e.g., termites or borers).</p>",
